<title>UK: UK construction Q4 output up 0.6 pct-industry body.</title>
<headline>UK construction Q4 output up 0.6 pct-industry body.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>British construction output rose 0.4 percent in 1996 and rose 0.6 percent in the fourth quarter of last year, showing the third consecutive quarterly rise, the Building Employers Confederation (BEC) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The BEC's latest quarterly construction trends survey also said that tender margins had strengthened for the second quarter in a row. All construction firms were now seen to be working at more than 50 percent of their full capacity.</p>
</text>
